Spotlight Effect — Art Deco reel (Tagalog) · asset sources & licences

Music        Original score, synthesised in code (score.py, numpy). No samples.
Sound FX     Synthesised in code (score.py). No samples.
Voice        None: the story is told in Tagalog on-screen text (burned-in cards + spotlight-effect.srt).
Fonts        Limelight (Eben Sorkin), Poiret One (Denis Masharov), Josefin Sans (Santiago Orozco), Italiana (Santiago Orozco)
             — Google Fonts, SIL Open Font License 1.1. Unmodified copies from github.com/google/fonts (ofl/), licences in fonts/.
Artwork      All characters, sets and props drawn procedurally in code (chars.js / main.js).
Engine       engine/ (deco.js, type.js, bulbs.js, cam.js) copied from the Art Deco style of the Lemo-Opuscar library
             (MIT License, github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar).
Fact         Gilovich, T., Medvec, V. H., & Savitsky, K. (2000). The spotlight effect in social judgment.
             Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 78(2), 211–222. Cited on screen.
Style        Art Deco grammar (Cassandre posters, Busby Berkeley overheads). Nothing copied from any poster, film or building.
